| # `.ONESHELL` makes one script of the whole recipe, and GNU Make takes nothing
| # off the end of a line of it: `chop_commands` (commands.c) never chopped the
| # recipe, and the one-shell branch of `construct_command_argv_internal` (job.c)
| # strips only the blanks and `[@+-]` that stand at the START of an interior
| # line.
| #
| # A here-document is where that stops being invisible, because there the script
| # is reading its own text: the blanks a line ends on are written into the file.
| # GNU Make 4.4.1 writes `line one` with the space after it; a build that tidies
| # the end of the line writes a different file.
| .ONESHELL:
| SP = $(subst x, ,x)
| all:
| 	@cat <<'BODY' > out
| 	line one$(SP)
| 	line two
| 	BODY
